Libre AI ai-practices is a multi-licence repository.

The licence for each file is declared through SPDX metadata and REUSE.toml:

- EUPL-1.2: first-party applications, crates, runtime code, repository
  automation under `.github/` and operational prompts;
- Apache-2.0: JSON Schema contracts, test fixtures, build tooling and the
  generated Libre AI design-system output vendored under
  `apps/web/assets/` and `crates/ui/assets/` (`tokens.css`, `themes.css`,
  `components.css` and the `libre-ia/` build records);
- CC-BY-4.0: editorial documentation, the pedagogical content corpus and
  first-party project records;
- upstream terms: third-party and vendored material.

One class of third-party material is carved out of every declaration above:

- the self-hosted fonts under `apps/web/assets/fonts/` and
  `crates/ui/assets/fonts/` remain OFL-1.1, under the copyright of their
  respective project authors.

Full licence texts are stored in LICENSES/.

The organization-wide licensing policy — scope, precedence, historical grants,
data and contribution rules — is the canonical one and is not restated here:
https://github.com/libre-ai/libre-ai/blob/main/LICENSING.md

Historical revisions of this repository previously published under MIT remain
available under those terms. No previous licence grant is withdrawn.
